concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-2-sec-13-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13 Section 13"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-13-2 ;
    values:originalText "3(3) of the Criminal Code). Defence for not giving reverse mortgage information statement  (5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d), and of subsection (2) so far as it relates to that paragraph, it is a defence if the licensee reasonably believes that another person has given the consumer a reverse mortgage information statement in the last 90 days. Note: For the purposes of subsection (2), a defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5) (see subsection" ;
    skos:definition "3(3) of the Criminal Code). Defence for not giving reverse mortgage information statement  (5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d), and of subsection (2) so far as it relates to that paragraph, it is a defence if the licensee reasonably believes that another person has given the consumer a reverse mortgage information statement in the last 90 days. Note: For the purposes of subsection (2), a defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5) (see subsection"@en ;
