doc:sch-2-sec-133dd-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "133DD(3) Making reverse mortgage information statement available in" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (2); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct contravenes the requirement. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. Defences" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-2-sec-133dd-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133DD(4) Making reverse mortgage information statement available in"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-133dd-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (3), it is a defence if:  (a) the licensee has given the consumer, or reasonably believes that someone else has given the consumer, a reverse mortgage information statement; or  (b) the licensee:  (i) is a credit provider under one or more credit contracts for reverse mortgages; and  (ii) reasonably believes that the consumer would not be eligible to make a credit contract with the licensee for a reverse mortgage; or  (c) there exist circumstances prescribed by regulations as circumstances in which the licensee is not required to give the consumer a reverse mortgage information statement. Note: For the purposes of subsection (3), a defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (4) (see subsection" ;
    skos:definition "(4) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (3), it is a defence if:  (a) the licensee has given the consumer, or reasonably believes that someone else has given the consumer, a reverse mortgage information statement; or  (b) the licensee:  (i) is a credit provider under one or more credit contracts for reverse mortgages; and  (ii) reasonably believes that the consumer would not be eligible to make a credit contract with the licensee for a reverse mortgage; or  (c) there exist circumstances prescribed by regulations as circumstances in which the licensee is not required to give the consumer a reverse mortgage information statement. Note: For the purposes of subsection (3), a defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (4) (see subsection"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7768f4412752033008133c880b498192e92184234266378223173f956b9839c1" ;
    values:partOf concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-2-sec-133dd ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Licensee must provide reverse mortgage information statement under certain circumstances." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
