doc:sch-3-sec-124a-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "124A(1) Prohibition on providing credit assistance in relation to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A licensee must not provide credit assistance to a consumer by:  (a) suggesting that the consumer apply, or assisting the consumer to apply, for a short-term credit contract; or  (b) suggesting that the consumer apply, or assisting the consumer to apply, for an increase to the credit limit of a particular short-term credit contract with a particular credit provider. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units. Offence" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer .

concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-3-sec-124a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "124A(2) Prohibition on providing credit assistance in relation to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-124a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Short-term and small amount credit contracts  Schedule 3  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (1); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct contravenes the requirement. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Short-term and small amount credit contracts  Schedule 3  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (1); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct contravenes the requirement. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units."@en ;
