doc:sch-3-sec-133cc-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "133CC(1) Licensee must not enter into a small amount credit contract" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A licensee must not enter into, or offer to enter into, a small amount credit contract with a consumer who will be the debtor under the contract if:  (a) the consumer is included in a class of consumers prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) the repayments that would be required under the contract would not meet the requirements prescribed by the regulations. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units. Note: For example, the regulations may provide that the amount of a repayment must not exceed a specified percentage of the consumer’s income. Offence" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-3-sec-133cc-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133CC(2) Licensee must not enter into a small amount credit contract"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-133cc-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (1); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct contravenes the requirement. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection (1); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct contravenes the requirement. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units."@en ;
