concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-24a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24A Offences related to prohibited monetary obligations—credit"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-24a ;
    values:originalText "assistance providers  (1) A person must not provide credit assistance to a consumer by: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  Schedule 4  (a) suggesting that the consumer apply for a particular small amount credit contract with a particular credit provider; or  (b) assisting the consumer to apply for a particular small amount credit contract with a particular credit provider; if the person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the contract will contravene subsection 23A(1). Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (2) If a person provides credit assistance to a consumer that is prohibited by subsection (1):  (a) the consumer is not liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to pay any fees or charges to the person in relation to:  (i) the credit assistance; or  (ii) any other services provided by the person in connection with the credit assistance; and  (b) the consumer may recover as a debt due to the consumer the amount of any such fees or charges paid by the consumer to the person." ;
    skos:definition "assistance providers  (1) A person must not provide credit assistance to a consumer by: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  Schedule 4  (a) suggesting that the consumer apply for a particular small amount credit contract with a particular credit provider; or  (b) assisting the consumer to apply for a particular small amount credit contract with a particular credit provider; if the person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the contract will contravene subsection 23A(1). Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (2) If a person provides credit assistance to a consumer that is prohibited by subsection (1):  (a) the consumer is not liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to pay any fees or charges to the person in relation to:  (i) the credit assistance; or  (ii) any other services provided by the person in connection with the credit assistance; and  (b) the consumer may recover as a debt due to the consumer the amount of any such fees or charges paid by the consumer to the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "78d6a1feb039e168b90bb31355fde2596f0cd1a7ff296f35beeda4ecc982cc80" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-24a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
