concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32A Prohibitions relating to credit contracts if the annual cost rate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-32a ;
    values:originalText "exceeds 48% Entering into a credit contract  (1) A credit provider must not enter into a credit contract if the annual cost rate of the contract exceeds 48%. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. Provision of credit assistance  (2) A person must not provide credit assistance to a consumer by suggesting that the consumer apply, or assisting the consumer to apply, for a particular credit contract with a particular credit ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 4  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  provider if the person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the annual cost rate of the contract exceeds 48%. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (3) If a person provides credit assistance to a consumer that is prohibited by subsection (2):  (a) the consumer is not liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to pay any fees or charges to the person in relation to:  (i) the credit assistance; or  (ii) any other services provided by the person in connection with the credit assistance; and  (b) the consumer may recover as a debt due to the consumer the amount of any such fees or charges paid by the consumer to the person. Application  (4) This section does not apply if:  (a) the credit provider is an ADI; or  (b) the credit contract is a small amount credit contract or bridging finance contract." ;
    skos:definition "exceeds 48% Entering into a credit contract  (1) A credit provider must not enter into a credit contract if the annual cost rate of the contract exceeds 48%. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. Provision of credit assistance  (2) A person must not provide credit assistance to a consumer by suggesting that the consumer apply, or assisting the consumer to apply, for a particular credit contract with a particular credit ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 4  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  provider if the person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the annual cost rate of the contract exceeds 48%. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (3) If a person provides credit assistance to a consumer that is prohibited by subsection (2):  (a) the consumer is not liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to pay any fees or charges to the person in relation to:  (i) the credit assistance; or  (ii) any other services provided by the person in connection with the credit assistance; and  (b) the consumer may recover as a debt due to the consumer the amount of any such fees or charges paid by the consumer to the person. Application  (4) This section does not apply if:  (a) the credit provider is an ADI; or  (b) the credit contract is a small amount credit contract or bridging finance contract."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "223311f472f11b4eeab208c3f69ade113ae5fc6c5c889264f5b45f86f94b60f8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32a-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32a-ss-3 ;
