doc:sch-4-sec-32a-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32A(4) Prohibitions relating to credit contracts if the annual cost rate" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) This section does not apply if:  (a) the credit provider is an ADI; or  (b) the credit contract is a small amount credit contract or bridging finance contract." ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer .

concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32AA Prohibition relating to the annual cost rate of credit"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-32aa ;
    values:originalText "contracts—later increases of the annual percentage rate etc.  (1) If:  (a) a credit provider is a party to a credit contract (other than a small amount credit contract or bridging finance contract); and  (b) the credit provider is not an ADI; and  (c) either or both of the following things (the varied matters) occur after the contract is entered into:  (i) the annual percentage rate under the contract increases;  (ii) an amount referred to in subsection 32B(3) that is prescribed by the regulations increases; the credit provider contravenes this subsection if the annual cost rate of the contract would have exceeded 48% at the time the contract was entered into if that or those varied matters had been ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  Schedule 4  taken into account at that time for the purposes of calculating the annual cost rate of the contract.  (2) A credit provider must not contravene subsection (1). Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "contracts—later increases of the annual percentage rate etc.  (1) If:  (a) a credit provider is a party to a credit contract (other than a small amount credit contract or bridging finance contract); and  (b) the credit provider is not an ADI; and  (c) either or both of the following things (the varied matters) occur after the contract is entered into:  (i) the annual percentage rate under the contract increases;  (ii) an amount referred to in subsection 32B(3) that is prescribed by the regulations increases; the credit provider contravenes this subsection if the annual cost rate of the contract would have exceeded 48% at the time the contract was entered into if that or those varied matters had been ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  Schedule 4  taken into account at that time for the purposes of calculating the annual cost rate of the contract.  (2) A credit provider must not contravene subsection (1). Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2cfec8055ad331d3b9182e15ba7d3542bacc0516c28f3076eafed4010406e401" ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32aa-ss-1 ;
