concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32b-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32B(6) Calculation of annual cost rate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-32b-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) In calculating the annual cost rate, reasonable approximations may be made if it would be impractical or unreasonably onerous to make a precise calculation. Example: If repayments are to be made on a fixed day each month, it may be assumed that repayments will be made on that day each month even though the credit contract provides for payment on the preceding or succeeding business day when the due date is not a business day." ;
    skos:definition "(6) In calculating the annual cost rate, reasonable approximations may be made if it would be impractical or unreasonably onerous to make a precise calculation. Example: If repayments are to be made on a fixed day each month, it may be assumed that repayments will be made on that day each month even though the credit contract provides for payment on the preceding or succeeding business day when the due date is not a business day."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f2899f26499983aa81745a54f865c8aad17f30ff48f7c51ddac14978d15d51f2" ;
    values:partOf concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32b ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Reasonable approximations may be made in calculating annual cost rate." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
