concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32b-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32B(8) Calculation of annual cost rate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-32b-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) If the credit contract is a continuing credit contract, the following assumptions also apply to the calculation of the annual cost rate of the contract:  (a) that the debtor has drawn down the maximum amount of credit that the credit provider has agreed to provide under the contract;  (b) that the debtor will pay the minimum repayments specified in the contract; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 4  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  (c) if credit is provided in respect of payment by the credit provider to a third person in relation to goods or services or cash supplied by that third person to the debtor from time to time—that the debtor will not be supplied with any further goods or services or cash;  (d) if credit is provided in respect of cash supplied by the credit provider to the debtor from time to time—that the debtor will not be supplied with any further cash." ;
    skos:definition "(8) If the credit contract is a continuing credit contract, the following assumptions also apply to the calculation of the annual cost rate of the contract:  (a) that the debtor has drawn down the maximum amount of credit that the credit provider has agreed to provide under the contract;  (b) that the debtor will pay the minimum repayments specified in the contract; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 4  Caps on costs etc. for credit contracts  (c) if credit is provided in respect of payment by the credit provider to a third person in relation to goods or services or cash supplied by that third person to the debtor from time to time—that the debtor will not be supplied with any further goods or services or cash;  (d) if credit is provided in respect of cash supplied by the credit provider to the debtor from time to time—that the debtor will not be supplied with any further cash."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "47b486e52973e98af6353b05978737f4f4453aadd691e21ee31fad18a1aeccb2" ;
    values:partOf concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-4-sec-32b ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Debtor must pay minimum repayments and not be supplied with further goods or services or cash." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf, p.67" ;
