concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Subsection 199(2) (at the end of the table)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-8 ;
    values:originalText "Add: Section 175F of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  by the regulations—that higher amount. Subsection 175G(6) of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Section 177D of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 177E of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 177F of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Section 179K of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 179Q of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Subsection 179R(3) of the National Credit Code the order is for an amount that is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount." ;
    skos:definition "Add: Section 175F of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  by the regulations—that higher amount. Subsection 175G(6) of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Section 177D of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 177E of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 177F of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Section 179K of the National Credit Code not applicable. Section 179Q of the National Credit Code the value of the consumer lease to which the order relates is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount. Subsection 179R(3) of the National Credit Code the order is for an amount that is not more than: (a) $40,000; or (b) if a higher amount is prescribed by the regulations—that higher amount."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0fb4464fd0b06090c1607cf49333bf170e68a6e000f81694f5872b0e67068863" ;
    cof:pageNumber "75"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Maximum value of consumer lease" ;
    dc:description "$40,000 or higher amount prescribed by regulations" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
