concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "175C Statements of account"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-175c ;
    values:originalText "(1) A lessor must give to the lessee, or arrange for the lessee to be given, periodic statements of account in accordance with this Subdivision. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (2) The maximum period for a statement of account is 12 months.  (3) A statement of account need not be given if:  (a) the lessee was in default under the consumer lease during the statement period and the lessor has commenced enforcement proceedings; or  (b) the lessee has died or is insolvent and the lessee’s personal representative or trustee in bankruptcy has not requested a statement of account.  (4) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A lessor must give to the lessee, or arrange for the lessee to be given, periodic statements of account in accordance with this Subdivision. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (2) The maximum period for a statement of account is 12 months.  (3) A statement of account need not be given if:  (a) the lessee was in default under the consumer lease during the statement period and the lessor has commenced enforcement proceedings; or  (b) the lessee has died or is insolvent and the lessee’s personal representative or trustee in bankruptcy has not requested a statement of account.  (4) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cdfad4bb0d083cd8bf4b802b5b0dcccb5a3928f49bf38b0265096e691611cdfa" ;
    cof:pageNumber "79"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175c-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175c-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf, p.79" .
doc:sch-5-sec-175c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "175C Statements of account" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A lessor must give to the lessee, or arrange for the lessee to be given, periodic statements of account in accordance with this Subdivision. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (2) The maximum period for a statement of account is 12 months.  (3) A statement of account need not be given if:  (a) the lessee was in default under the consumer lease during the statement period and the lessor has commenced enforcement proceedings; or  (b) the lessee has died or is insolvent and the lessee’s personal representative or trustee in bankruptcy has not requested a statement of account.  (4) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases" ;
    cof:pageNumber "79"^^xsd:integer .

