concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-175h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "175H End of lease statement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-175h ;
    values:originalText "(1) A lessor must arrange for the lessee to be given, not later than 90 days before the end of the fixed term of a consumer lease, a statement containing the information prescribed by the regulations. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances (if any) prescribed by the regulations.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A lessor must arrange for the lessee to be given, not later than 90 days before the end of the fixed term of a consumer lease, a statement containing the information prescribed by the regulations. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances (if any) prescribed by the regulations.  (3) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2d3c7b12317b153c9ba67127ad880b9b71ad01e2b3556163305b79c293d95625" ;
