concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179C One-off notice to be given the first time a direct debit default"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179c ;
    values:originalText "occurs  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a lessee authorises payment of an amount for a consumer lease by direct debit; and  (b) default occurs; and  (c) it is the first occasion the default occurs.  (2) The lessor must give the lessee a notice, complying with this section, within 14 days of the default occurring. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  (3) The notice must contain the information prescribed by the regulations.  (4) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.  (5) This section does not affect any other requirement under this Code to give a notice. Subdivision C—Enforcement of consumer leases" ;
    skos:definition "occurs  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a lessee authorises payment of an amount for a consumer lease by direct debit; and  (b) default occurs; and  (c) it is the first occasion the default occurs.  (2) The lessor must give the lessee a notice, complying with this section, within 14 days of the default occurring. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  (3) The notice must contain the information prescribed by the regulations.  (4) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.  (5) This section does not affect any other requirement under this Code to give a notice. Subdivision C—Enforcement of consumer leases"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ff62989ee65e826beb299bec384dbe5b3558db32dd724a75ee85ccbac9325cb0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "92"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179c-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf, p.92" .
doc:sch-5-sec-179c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179C One-off notice to be given the first time a direct debit default" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "occurs  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a lessee authorises payment of an amount for a consumer lease by direct debit; and  (b) default occurs; and  (c) it is the first occasion the default occurs.  (2) The lessor must give the lessee a notice, complying with this section, within 14 days of the default occurring. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  (3) The notice must contain the information prescribed by the regulations.  (4) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.  (5) This section does not affect any other requirement under this Code to give a notice. Subdivision C—Enforcement of consumer leases" ;
    cof:pageNumber "92"^^xsd:integer .

