    skos:definition "(1) A lessor must not begin enforcement proceedings against a lessee in relation to a consumer lease unless:  (a) the lessee is in default under the lease; and  (b) the lessor has given the lessee a default notice, complying with this section, allowing the lessee a period of at least 30 days from the date of the notice to remedy the default; and  (c) the default has not been remedied within that period. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units. Note: If a lessee has given a lessor a hardship notice or a postponement request there may be extra requirements that the lessor must comply with before beginning enforcement proceedings—see sections 179F and 179H. Default notice requirements"@en ;
