    skos:definition "(4) However, the lessor may take possession of goods hired under the consumer lease if the lessor reasonably believes that:  (a) the lessee has removed or disposed of the goods, or intends to remove or dispose of them; or  (b) urgent action is necessary to protect the goods. Strict liability"@en ;
