concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179J Effect of negotiated postponement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179j ;
    values:originalText "(1) A default notice under section 179D is taken, for the purposes of this Code, not to have been given if a postponement is negotiated with the lessor under section 179H and the lessee complies with the conditions of postponement.  (2) A lessor must give written notice of the conditions of a postponement referred to in subsection (1) not later than 30 days ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  after agreement is reached on the postponement. The notice must set out the consequences under subsection (5) if the conditions of the postponement are not complied with. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.  (4) A lessor that is required to give notice under section 177A (which deals with changes to leases by agreement) in relation to a postponement is not required to comply with subsection (2).  (5) If any of the conditions of a postponement are not complied with, a lessor is not required to give a further default notice under this Code to the lessee with whom the postponement was negotiated before proceeding with enforcement proceedings." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A default notice under section 179D is taken, for the purposes of this Code, not to have been given if a postponement is negotiated with the lessor under section 179H and the lessee complies with the conditions of postponement.  (2) A lessor must give written notice of the conditions of a postponement referred to in subsection (1) not later than 30 days ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  after agreement is reached on the postponement. The notice must set out the consequences under subsection (5) if the conditions of the postponement are not complied with. Criminal penalty: 100 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.  (4) A lessor that is required to give notice under section 177A (which deals with changes to leases by agreement) in relation to a postponement is not required to comply with subsection (2).  (5) If any of the conditions of a postponement are not complied with, a lessor is not required to give a further default notice under this Code to the lessee with whom the postponement was negotiated before proceeding with enforcement proceedings."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d11dfefa99cc7af333afba7d6351d48b8c44c8d8068dd60abd4966cd7012eced" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179j-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
