concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179K Postponement by court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179k ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the lessee is unable to negotiate a postponement, the lessee may apply to the court for a postponement.  (2) After allowing the applicant and the lessor a reasonable opportunity to be heard, the court may:  (a) order the postponement to which the application relates; or  (b) refuse to order the postponement; or  (c) make such other orders as it thinks fit.  (3) The court may, if it thinks it appropriate in the circumstances, stay any enforcement proceedings under the consumer lease until the application has been determined." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the lessee is unable to negotiate a postponement, the lessee may apply to the court for a postponement.  (2) After allowing the applicant and the lessor a reasonable opportunity to be heard, the court may:  (a) order the postponement to which the application relates; or  (b) refuse to order the postponement; or  (c) make such other orders as it thinks fit.  (3) The court may, if it thinks it appropriate in the circumstances, stay any enforcement proceedings under the consumer lease until the application has been determined."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8154202ee001e7d713e8985cde2c610b523806bec583cb5a5670fa86d94f4c00" ;
    cof:pageNumber "99"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179k-ss-1 ;
