concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179L Lessor may apply for variation of postponement order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179l ;
    values:originalText "(1) A lessor that is subject to an order under this Subdivision may apply to the court for variation of the order.  (2) On such an application, the court may:  (a) vary the order to which the application relates as it thinks fit; or  (b) refuse to vary the order; or  (c) revoke the order. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  Subdivision E—Enforcement procedures for goods hired under a consumer lease" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A lessor that is subject to an order under this Subdivision may apply to the court for variation of the order.  (2) On such an application, the court may:  (a) vary the order to which the application relates as it thinks fit; or  (b) refuse to vary the order; or  (c) revoke the order. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  Subdivision E—Enforcement procedures for goods hired under a consumer lease"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2c26c325a31ecaca14334daee1a8b060b8295cfdd4a5d133b8b1d6e81f1dea06" ;
    cof:pageNumber "99"^^xsd:integer ;
