concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179m a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179M Information as to location of goods hired under a consumer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179m ;
    values:originalText "lease  (1) A lessor may, by written notice to a lessee, require the lessee to inform the lessor, within 7 days after the day the notice is given to the lessee, where the goods hired under the consumer lease are and, if the goods are not in the lessee’s possession, to give the lessor all information in the lessee’s possession that might assist the lessor to trace the goods.  (2) A lessee who contravenes a notice under this section commits an offence. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "lease  (1) A lessor may, by written notice to a lessee, require the lessee to inform the lessor, within 7 days after the day the notice is given to the lessee, where the goods hired under the consumer lease are and, if the goods are not in the lessee’s possession, to give the lessor all information in the lessee’s possession that might assist the lessor to trace the goods.  (2) A lessee who contravenes a notice under this section commits an offence. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b544a7686d1186680a9d8f24ff542b00d8ae60da4dd2613a38f6292a8337cc37" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179m-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179m-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179m-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf, p.100" .
doc:sch-5-sec-179m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179M Information as to location of goods hired under a consumer" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "lease  (1) A lessor may, by written notice to a lessee, require the lessee to inform the lessor, within 7 days after the day the notice is given to the lessee, where the goods hired under the consumer lease are and, if the goods are not in the lessee’s possession, to give the lessor all information in the lessee’s possession that might assist the lessor to trace the goods.  (2) A lessee who contravenes a notice under this section commits an offence. Criminal penalty: 50 penalty units.  (3) Subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer .

