concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179r-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179R(3) Recovery of enforcement expenses"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179r-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If there is a dispute between the lessor and the lessee about the amount of enforcement expenses that may be recovered by the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  lessor, the court may, on application by any of the parties to the dispute, determine the amount of that liability." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If there is a dispute between the lessor and the lessee about the amount of enforcement expenses that may be recovered by the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Schedule 5  Consumer leases  lessor, the court may, on application by any of the parties to the dispute, determine the amount of that liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9aa6254cff6f9625eb69dd3b9f3f2a4a89fa2fe1dc67c54de63a7afb916b487b" ;
