concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179s a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179S Linked lessors and tied consumer leases"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-179s ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Code, a linked lessor of a supplier means a lessor:  (a) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding relating to:  (i) the supply to the supplier of goods in which the supplier deals; or  (ii) the business carried on by the supplier of supplying goods; or  (iii) the provision to persons of a consumer lease for the hire of goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; or  (b) to whom the supplier, by arrangement with the lessor, regularly refers persons for the purpose of being provided with a consumer lease; or  (c) whose forms of contract or forms of application or offers for a consumer lease are, by arrangement with the lessor, made available to persons by the supplier; or  (d) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding under which applications for a consumer lease or offers to be provided with a consumer lease from the lessor may be signed by persons at the premises of the supplier.  (2) A tied consumer lease is a consumer lease entered into between a lessor and a lessee where:  (a) the lessee enters into the lease to hire goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; and  (b) at the time the lease is entered into the lessor is a linked lessor of the supplier. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  Subdivision B—Liability of lessors for suppliers’ misrepresentations" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Code, a linked lessor of a supplier means a lessor:  (a) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding relating to:  (i) the supply to the supplier of goods in which the supplier deals; or  (ii) the business carried on by the supplier of supplying goods; or  (iii) the provision to persons of a consumer lease for the hire of goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; or  (b) to whom the supplier, by arrangement with the lessor, regularly refers persons for the purpose of being provided with a consumer lease; or  (c) whose forms of contract or forms of application or offers for a consumer lease are, by arrangement with the lessor, made available to persons by the supplier; or  (d) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding under which applications for a consumer lease or offers to be provided with a consumer lease from the lessor may be signed by persons at the premises of the supplier.  (2) A tied consumer lease is a consumer lease entered into between a lessor and a lessee where:  (a) the lessee enters into the lease to hire goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; and  (b) at the time the lease is entered into the lessor is a linked lessor of the supplier. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  Subdivision B—Liability of lessors for suppliers’ misrepresentations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "63043ed72f5fecfd5c900a7d289495b52d26e3b0c9198856c46ca40fd683b885" ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179s-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012-sch-5-sec-179s-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "consumer-credit-legislation-amendment-enhancements-act-2012.pdf, p.102" .
doc:sch-5-sec-179s a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179S Linked lessors and tied consumer leases" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Code, a linked lessor of a supplier means a lessor:  (a) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding relating to:  (i) the supply to the supplier of goods in which the supplier deals; or  (ii) the business carried on by the supplier of supplying goods; or  (iii) the provision to persons of a consumer lease for the hire of goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; or  (b) to whom the supplier, by arrangement with the lessor, regularly refers persons for the purpose of being provided with a consumer lease; or  (c) whose forms of contract or forms of application or offers for a consumer lease are, by arrangement with the lessor, made available to persons by the supplier; or  (d) with whom the supplier has a contract, arrangement or understanding under which applications for a consumer lease or offers to be provided with a consumer lease from the lessor may be signed by persons at the premises of the supplier.  (2) A tied consumer lease is a consumer lease entered into between a lessor and a lessee where:  (a) the lessee enters into the lease to hire goods supplied by the supplier to the lessor; and  (b) at the time the lease is entered into the lessor is a linked lessor of the supplier. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00130  Consumer leases  Schedule 5  Subdivision B—Liability of lessors for suppliers’ misrepresentations" ;
    cof:pageNumber "102"^^xsd:integer .

